Today I solved leetcode question 2326: Spiral Matrix IV.

Description: Question states that we are given a linked list with values and we should put that values in m x n matrix.
              And if we do not have sufficient values then we must put -1 in empty places.
              And we must place our values in spiral format.
              eg- list=[1,2,3,4,5,6] m=3 n=3
                ans=  [1   2  3]
                      [-1 -1  4] 
                      [-1  6  5]

Solution: We first create five variables. top, bottom, left, right and temp.
          top and left will have values 0. bottom will have value m-1 and right will have value n-1. temp will point to head.
          We will create answer matrix with pre assigned values of -1.
          Then we will start our while loop till top is less than equal to bottom and left is less than equal to right and temp is not equal to null.
          
          Now we will start our first for loop.
          Our starting will be left and it will run till it is less than equal to right.
          And inside it we will assign values at index [top][i] the value of temp if it is not null.
          And then we will move temp to next node. If temp is equal to null we will do nothing.
          Then after the loop we will increase top by 1.
          
          Now we will start oue second loop which will start from top and run till bottom.
          Inside it we will assign the values at index [i][right] the value of temp if it is not null. And we will move temp to next node.
          If null then we will do nothing. And then we will decrease right by 1.
          
          Now we will start our third loop which will start from right and run till left.
          Inside this loop we will assign the values at index [bottom][i] the value of temp if it is not null.
          And we will move temp to next node. And if it is null we will do nothing.
          And at last we will decrease bottom by 1.

          Now we will start our final loop which will start from bottom and run till top.
          We will assign values at index [i][left] the value of temp if it is not null. And we will move temp to next node.
          And if it is null we will do nothing. Now we will increase left by 1.

          Our solution runs in a spiral cycle which matrix getting smaller from each side at a time.
